<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1 The above Statement of Unaudited financial results are prepared, published as per  Reg 33 of the SEBI  LODR  2015, as amended. These financial results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on August 24, 2020. These  Unaudited results are prepared in accordance with the Ind AS as prescribed u/s 133 of the Co Act, 2013, read with the relevant Rules thereunder.   n2 The figures for the qe Mar 31 2020 are the balancing figures between audited figures of the full F.Y  ended March 31, 2020 and the published ytd figures up to the end of Dec 19 .  n3 The Company is  engaged in manufacture of Rubber Chemicals, which in the context of Ind AS 108, constitutes a single reportable segment.  n4 The Unaudited consolidated financial results of NOCIL Limited have been prepared as per Ind AS 110 -, Financial results of the WOS company, PIL Chemicals Limited, have been consolidated with NOCIL .  n5 The Board has approved a proposed Scheme of Amalgamation of Suremi and Sushripada with NOCIL U/S 230-232 of the Cos Act, 2013, subject to obtaining various statutory approvals. Pursuant to the Scheme becoming effective, the shareholders of Suremi and Sushripada will be alloted 2,12,72,165 and 89,60,880 equity shares in lieu of  equity shares in NOCIL Limited currently held by Suremi and Sushripada respectively. There will be no change in the shareholding of the Promoter Group and Public Shareholders of NOCIL Limited.  n6 The Co.s operations were shut down from end March 2020 due to nationwide lockdown in view of the COVID-19. The Company's plants have since resumed operations in  a phased manner taking all due care for the health and safety of its employees. Due to  the lockdown the performance of the Company for  qtr was impacted by reduction in the volumes, revenue and profits. Management has assessed  the current situation and does not envisage any impact on the going concern assumption in the foreseeable future. The impact of COVID-19 is a continual process. The financial implications are contingent on the business parameters emerging from time to time .The Co will continue to closely monitor any material changes from those estimated as on the date of adoption of this financial results.  n7 The figures for the corresponding previous periods have been regrouped / restated, wherever necessary to conform with current period's classification</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
